			<div class="content" id="post-content-4835478">
									

<p><strong>Seeking Greenlights:</strong> Yes</p>
<p><strong>Page Type:</strong> SCP Article/Joke SCP</p>
<p><strong>Genre (Optional):</strong> Other (Meta)</p>
<p><strong>Page Layout (Optional):</strong> Description and Containment Article</p>
<p><strong>Elevator Pitch:</strong> Reality Warper who can digitally transfer his consciousness through various realities, and as a result becomes a Virtual Tuber &quot;VTuber&quot; in our reality.</p>
<p><strong>Central Narrative:</strong> Due to being cast out from his body in a containment attempt by the foundation, His consciousness created a virtual body in our reality, Where he has learned extensively about the Foundation through the Wiki. Though originally classified as safe, the foundation reclassified him as Euclid due to the potential of Memetic SCP Containment breaches and broken masquerade situations. He is aware that the SCP Universe is considered Fictional in our reality and has used this to learn as much about it as he can.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;show&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p><strong>Hook/Attention-Grabber:</strong> It's an Anomalous VTuber, which (hopefully) will also have a real life presence on twitch, making it Unique, Interesting, and Interactive</p>
<p><strong>Additional Notes:</strong> I am not entirely sure how an idea such as this would fit into the SCP Universe, nor how I should write it exactly. I would love any suggestions or input on the functional application of this concept.</p>
<p>As mentioned above, I have full intention of turning this concept into an actual VTuber on Twitch, which brings in another side of this which I don't believe has ever been done before. It also raises a question about the ethical nature such a concept, since VTubers and streamers often make money on their platforms, and the SCP universe being in a strange gray area concerning copyright and monetization. Due to the nature of such platforms, the actual SCP content would not be directly monetized, but I'm curious to hear other peoples thoughts on this topic.</p>
<p>Just to be clear, I am not doing this in hopes of launching a VTuber career off the back of the SCP universe. I had planned on Creating a VTuber for awhile now and was trying to come up with an interesting backstory. This just kind of clicked for me, though it would just be the backstory and may not actually contribute to the active stream very often. It will be a variety stream of music, gaming and other activities.</p>
<p>Monetization is not the goal, I just wanted to create a cool character and expose people to 2 communities that I love. (VTubers and The SCP Foundation).</p>
</div>
